Z||000000||286SE'S||12-10-2001||12:34 PM||||Got into my car this morning and put the clutch pedal to the floor and turned the key and the car lurched forward. Oh no what is this puddle of brake fluid on the floor mat?<BR>Time for a new master cylinder.<BR>Anyone got the part number for the 86 clutch master cylinder? It is a 5 speed isuzu 4 cyl.<BR>I have searched the archives and all those who has asked this question before did not get a reply. I need the GM original not an aftermarket product that The Fieros store sells.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000001||Archie||12-10-2001||01:02 PM||||10079730 is the one I use.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||PK||12-10-2001||03:46 PM||||There are two types of master for the '86:<P>1) Pipe attached behind the resevoir = 10142033.<P>2) Pipe attached infront of resevoir = 10079730.<P>Cheers<BR>PK in the UK<P><BR>  <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 286SE'S:<BR><B>Got into my car this morning and put the clutch pedal to the floor and turned the key and the car lurched forward. Oh no what is this puddle of brake fluid on the floor mat?<BR>Time for a new master cylinder.<BR>Anyone got the part number for the 86 clutch master cylinder? It is a 5 speed isuzu 4 cyl.<BR>I have searched the archives and all those who has asked this question before did not get a reply. I need the GM original not an aftermarket product that The Fieros store sells.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Terry</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Archie||12-10-2001||04:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PK:<BR><B>There are two types of master for the '86:<P>1) Pipe attached behind the resevoir = 10142033.<P>2) Pipe attached infront of resevoir = 10079730.<P>Cheers<BR>PK in the UK<P>Yeah, I think the 10142033 was only used on the 4 speed cars and the 10079730 was on the 5 speed cars.<P>Archie<BR>  <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||286SE'S||12-10-2001||06:55 PM||||Thanks Archie and PK,<BR>I have my pipe in front of the reservoir so<BR>that sounds like the right one for the 5 speed.<BR>I have placed an order at GMPARTSDIRECT.com<BR>It was about $71 + shipping.<BR>I am so glad I found out about all the problems that other members have had with the non-GM masters before I ordered from the Fiero Store. This Forum is Great!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||PK||12-11-2001||02:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have a 4 speed 86 SE that has a type 2) master cylinder! Just arrived from gmpartsdirect along with a new slave.  They only accept US credit cards so I was lucky to have a very kind relative in the states who did all the ordering and passed it on!<P>Good luck with the parts.  Its well worth reading Archies bleeding instructions while your waiting for your parts to arrive.<P>Cheers <BR>PK<P>||||reg||1
